    "reason": "UCR offers relevant mathematics, programming, image analysis and Earth science. Leiden combines these tools with a sequence in physics and astronomy, telescope observation and a supervised astronomy research project. The available UCR courses do not provide that progression.",
    "curriculumContext": "The standalone Leiden BSc comprises 150 EC of required work and 30 EC of electives. The research project includes 18 EC of research, a 1 EC presentation and a 3 EC thesis.",
    "ucrCourseEvidence": "Mathematical Methods, Linear Algebra, Advanced Calculus, Computational & Numerical Methods, Linear Systems and Probability & Statistics support modelling and quantitative analysis. Programming, Machine Learning and Image Processing & Computer Vision support data analysis and image interpretation. Robotics contributes control, sensing and physical modelling in a robotics context. Dynamic Earth, Earth System Science Tools and Earth Observation offer terrestrial analogues for systems analysis and remote sensing. None of the tested directions supplies the cumulative core in physics and astrophysics, or observational and research practice on astronomical objects. Sustainability Essentials II includes waves, interference and optical spectroscopy, giving introductory physics overlap without the sequenced optics and observing laboratory.",
